  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0ATF">Lemma <span data-tag="0ATF">110.78.1</span>.</a> There exists a commutative ring $A$ and a flat $A$-algebra $B$ which cannot be written as a filtered colimit of finitely presented flat $A$-algebras. In fact, we may either choose $A$ to be a finite type $\mathbf{F}_ p$-algebra or a $1$-dimensional Noetherian local ring with residue field of characteristic $0$. </p>
